
### 5.3 Component responsibilities

```bash

# OpsNexus Components

## opsnexus-agent

The agent runs on monitored Linux systems.

Responsibilities:

- Collect CPU metrics
- Collect memory metrics
- Collect disk metrics
- Collect network metrics
- Collect system information
- Monitor Docker
- Execute approved automation tasks
- Report health and telemetry

## opsnexus-backend

The backend is the central control plane.

Responsibilities:

- Authentication
- Agent registration
- Device/server management
- Telemetry ingestion
- Monitoring state
- Automation orchestration
- Alert processing
- API services

Technology:

- Go

## opsnexus-dashboard

The web interface for operators.

Responsibilities:

- Infrastructure overview
- Server details
- Docker monitoring
- Alerts
- Automation controls
- System health

## opsnexus-common

Shared contracts used by Go components.

Examples:

- Agent models
- Telemetry models
- API request/response structures
- Event definitions
- Error models

## opsnexus-api

Contains API specifications and contracts.

The API repository should remain independent from backend implementation.

## opsnexus-cli

Command-line interface for interacting with OpsNexus.

Possible operations:

- Login
- Register agent
- List servers
- Inspect server
- View metrics
- Trigger automation

## opsnexus-deployment

Deployment infrastructure.

Examples:

- Docker Compose
- Container configurations
- Environment templates
- Deployment scripts
- Production infrastructure

## opsnexus-docs

Central project documentation.

## awesome-opsnexus

Community-oriented curated resources related to OpsNexus.
EOF